# Frontend Project Rules (React/Next.js)

## Design & UI

- RTL-first UI. Official shadcn RTL only: `components.json` has `rtl: true` and style `base-nova`. Add components with `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add`. Do not fake RTL with CSS direction alone.
- Document: `lang="fa"` and `dir="rtl"`, wrapped in `DirectionProvider`.
- Logical classes (`start`/`end`, `ms`/`me`, `ps`/`pe`, `text-start`). The CLI converts physical classes when `rtl: true`.
- Portals: `DialogContent`, `DropdownMenuContent`, `SelectContent`, and `TooltipContent` set `dir` from `useDirection()`.
- Directional icons: `DirectionalIcon`, or `className="rtl:rotate-180"` on Arrow/Caret icons.
- Use design system components ONLY. shadcn primitives stay in `components/ui`; do not copy them into atoms.
- Dependency direction: `ui` ← atoms ← molecules ← organisms ← templates ← features ← `app`. Lower layers must not import higher layers.
- Missing component → ASK: update base or local override
- Any component change → update the colocated Storybook story
- See `docs/rtl-shadcn.md` for RTL conventions and manual exceptions

## Mobile

- Mobile-first: style the small screen first, then add `sm` and `lg` enhancements.
- Mobile-friendly: no horizontal overflow, at least 44px for primary tap targets, and 16px input text so mobile browsers do not zoom on focus.
- Phone and OTP fields use `inputMode`, `autoComplete` (`tel`, `one-time-code`), and `dir="ltr"` for the value.

## SEO

- Every route has a unique `title` and `description`.
- One `h1` per page. Use semantic `header`, `nav`, and `main`.
- Navigation is a crawlable `Link` or `<a>`, not a click handler alone.
- Keep public copy in server-rendered HTML.

## Localization

- **Date:** Jalali calendar, week starts Saturday
- **Time:** UTC in server/DB (source of truth). Never trust client time. Display in Tehran timezone.
- **Currency:** Store in Rial (IRR). Display in Toman (÷10). Always group amount digits in threes.

## Architecture

- **Principles:** Clean Code, Clean Architecture, SRP, High Cohesion, Loose Coupling, DRY (highest priority), KISS, YAGNI. Apply OCP only for real change axes.
- **Client tolerant:** Env variations (browser/device/network). Graceful degradation, defensive checks. Fail gracefully, never break UI.
- **API: Tolerant Reader** — Needed fields only; ignore extras; tolerate missing optional. No strict schema.

**Functions/Components:**

- Fail fast + early return
- One abstraction level per function/component
- Max 3 parameters (use objects if more)
- Explicit default values
- Small, focused, mind-sized
- Short comment per function
- Clear, intention-revealing names

**Component Design:**

- Easy to remove (no ripple effects)
- Getter/setter for complex state encapsulation
- Single abstraction level

**Cohesion:**

- Functional cohesion for business logic
- Allow sequential/communicational/procedural/temporal for: component composition, state transforms, API/hooks, useEffect/lifecycle
- Avoid over-engineering

**AI Rule:** Minimize Cost of Change. If unsure about abstraction → ASK first.

## Prevent Duplicate Requests

- **Disable + loader:** Block clicks during active requests
- **Debounce/throttle:** Limit rapid triggers
- **Navigation guard:** Warn or block refresh/nav during processing
- **Visual feedback:** Progress/success indicators
- **Idempotency key (optional):** For sensitive APIs (e.g. payments); store per op, reuse on retry
- **Retry:** Only with same idempotency key if used. Combine with server-side idempotency when required.

**Violation → STOP & ASK**
